{
  "_readme": "Finance role taxonomy used by intel/taxonomy.py. Patterns are case-insensitive regex fragments. The loader wraps every fragment in word boundaries, turns ' ?' into optional separators and ' ' into one-or-more separators (space, hyphen, slash), so write 'sales (and|&) trading' rather than escaping. Signals: title hits weigh 4, department hits 2, description hits 1 each (distinct patterns, capped per category). company_priors add points when the employer type makes a category more likely, but only when the posting already carries a finance signal or a generic finance title word. associate_stage decides whether an untitled 'Associate' is entry-level (post-undergrad) or experienced (post-MBA / post-banking) in that category. Job families (non_finance_families) are matched on the title in order; software and data_ml carry specialties (subcategories) scored the same way, where title words before the first comma or dash count most, tie_priority settles ties and related specialties earn partial credit for each other.",
